  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hi!\nFor a while now, a popular finger tracking product called the Leap Motion has been used for VR applications. Most notably, some VRChat competitors have begun supporting it as well, as it's an easy \"DIY\" solution for finger tracking.\nLeap Motion has an SDK that can be imported into Unity to allow for native support in games, and this would be a feature that I think a lot of people could benefit from. I've seen similar threads constantly requested, some getting around 90 likes as well. (https://developer.leapmotion.com/unity)\n\n\nCurrently, to use the Leap Motion in game, people have to use a third party program that allows it to emulate an index controller, but this is difficult and isn't as perfect as having native support.  (https://github.com/SDraw/driver_leap)\nPlease allow this to become a possibility!",
